Drop into 1.GG (or equivalent)

In 1.RNA,


Create a new gro file (GG.gro). Here it's done by stripping out the other nucleotides from the longer chain, original_8_nucleotide.gro, including leading phosphate, patching in H5T at the top in the location that the P was, just above the first O5', and H3T at the bottom, just below the last O3'. Also have to change the number of atoms given in the second line.


Renumber the gro file: gmx editconf -f GG.gro -o GG_renum.gro.


Create a topology file: gmx pdb2gmx -f GG_renum.gro -p topol_GG.top, choosing "1. AMBER03 protein ..." and "7: None" for the water model. [If we want to run a trajectory here, we'd need to edit this file so that forcefield specifies the right address, and include ions, but we'll skip that step for now.]


Edit 1.align.sh so that it refers to GG_renum.gro, and executed it. This will create various aligned and shifted gro files. (Probably have to come back to this .sh file, possibly, to adjust these alignments.)


run Look_at_results.ipynb to inspect these configurations.


Now shift to 2.RNA+NA+SOL_dropdown and copy topol_GG.top over from 1.RNA. Editing this file:

...

; Include forcefield parameters
#include "/home/chemistry/MD/amber_na.ff/forcefield.itp"

[ moleculetype ]
; Name            nrexcl
RNA                 3

...


; Include water topology
#include "/home/chemistry/MD/amber_na.ff/tip4pd.itp"

; Include topology for ions
#include "/home/chemistry/MD/amber_na.ff/ions.itp"

[ system ]
; Name
GG

[ molecules ]
; Compound        #mols
RNA            1
NA             1
SOL         2880


Also need to populate this folder with a water slab (like "SOL_annealed.gro") and a sodium ion "NA.gro").

Now run "Constructing the system.ipynb", cycling back to modifying the shift and rotation in 1.align.sh so that the RNA is sitting atop the ice properly. The result of this is a file called System1.gro.


Now move up a level and create an index file using ./make_index.sh. 


Move back down to 2.RNA+NA+SOL_dropdown and run 1.grompp_dropdown.sh and 2.mdrun_dropdown.sh


To start a longer trajectory, copy over the key files (.mdp, .sh). Change the name of the .sh files (e.g., from 1.grompp_dropdown.sh to 1.grompp.sh). Also, edit the 1.grompp.sh file so that it picks up as a starting configuration the .gro file from the 2.RNA+NA+SOL_dropdown file (instead of System1.gro).







